ios: a canvas that lost its pixels gets them again

On an iPhone the inventory panel came back as bare stone with its tab selected: WebKit had dropped the side panel's
canvas pixels while the app was in the foreground (no visibilitychange, no contextrestored, no memory warning, no
crash in the app's log), and patch 0026 sends a PixMap's changed pixels only, so redrawing the same inventory sent
nothing; only another tab (most pixels different) painted it again, and even then the pixels the two tabs share stayed
blank. The world and the minimap draw every frame and get their whole frame every 100 draws; the side panel, the
chatbox, the title screen's pieces and the classic layout's frame pieces draw only when their content changes, so a
lost canvas stayed blank until then, also after the page was shown again (PixMap.invalidate only acts at a draw).

Now every frame the client calls PixMap.keepShown() for each PixMap on screen (the surfaces of the mobile layout, every
piece of the classic canvas in game, the title screen's): the frame it last sent goes to its canvas again, whole, when
2 s (KEEP_MS) have passed since it last went whole or the PixMaps were invalidated since (a page shown again: at once).
`paint` holds that frame converted, so it costs a putImageData and no conversion, and `shown` stays what the canvas
shows, so the rects after it stay right; it does not change PixMap.generation (no full 3D frame, patch 0029). A
retarget forgets it until the next draw (the new canvas, perhaps another position). Host API resendSurface(area): the
HUD sends a surface's frame at once when it shows the panel, the chatbox or the minimap again.

